## Exact decision

The coordinator asked: “Approve AR13-01–05 in the proposal for local synthetic implementation?” The repository owner replied **“Approved”**. This directly approves all five named choices; no amendments were supplied. It is not inferred from earlier general next-cycle requests.

Approved proposal revision: `d897b1d8cd27eea9a7f5225813626fd2e4f3dce0:specs/003-health-assessment/local-artifact-review-contract-proposal.md`; exact UTF-8 SHA256 `c243feb9aa705bdddd69a9c8ee476b25b6dc647bbbea938298a0f02ee1af90f6`. The five choices and detailed state/replay/source/compatibility semantics at that revision are authoritative.

| Decision | Approved boundary |
| --- | --- |
| AR13-01 | Assigned synthetic Consultant alone reviews/withdraws individual artifacts; other existing finding roles/actions unchanged. |
| AR13-02 | Separate exact-source Reviewed for planning attestation; immutable generated originals remain Unverified and no correctness/remediation/execution safety is established. |
| AR13-03 | Latest review becomes historical/Needs review after complete-source change; latest withdrawal remains Unverified; no cross-run carryover or automatic revival. |
| AR13-04 | Attributed append-only review/withdraw history, required reason, expected revision, scoped event replay and atomic receipt; no invalidation writes on reads. |
| AR13-05 | One new opt-in local profile/contract lock; all nine historical profiles retain bytes and behavior. |

## Execution authority and remaining boundaries

Proceed with the [Cycle13 implementation plan](../../plans/active/local-pilot-artifact-review-cycle-13.md) and [test plan](local-artifact-review-test-plan.md). Settle narrow internal module APIs, closed DTO/schema and source concurrency fence through technical engineering review before dependent implementation. Do not seek the same approval again. Agent review may verify implementation details within these choices; it cannot alter the approved semantics.

This approval permits one additive dedicated-fictional-database schema and local synthetic profile, not a customer/production migration, deployed permission, real identity/provider/source, artifact editing/execution, task conversion/workflow/CSV, report publication or release. Existing ADRs, audit/authorization policy and G1–G9 remain unchanged. Full local completion/UAT/Milestone7/TP018 are not accepted by approval. The task-export role discrepancy remains deferred to its separate contract.

## Human-board completion condition

The previous “Decide the consultant artifact-review contract” dependency is **CLOSED** by this exact owner decision. Link this record when changing the board card. Technical implementation/verification remains RUNNING/PENDING evidence; no new human dependency is manufactured for routine internal engineering details.
